=> ldap vs AD

a)LDAP

LDAP is a protocol.

It defines how applications and systems can communicate with a directory service.

Often used for directory queries/authentication integration.

b) Active Directory

Active Directory is a Microsoft directory service.

It stores and manages identities such as users, groups, and computers and provides many enterprise identity/security capabilities.

AD supports LDAP, among other protocols.

=> LDAP = Rules for communicating

Active Directory = A system that uses those rules. Provides identity, authentication, authorization and policy capabilities.


